      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 7: fitting k_h on sustained climbs (the clean way)",
      "text": "On sustained climbs k_h ≈ 0.96–1: the rider pays the full mg·Δh, so there is no uniform climbing discount; sustained climbing is only 54% of total ascent — the discount lives in rollers and noise — so the right correction is the per-profile deadband, not a scalar (cross-check: cf + 2 m deadband 3.5% vs canonical 5.2% vs scalar k_smooth 5.9%).",
      "appearance": [
        {
          "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/journal/MODEL_COMPARISON_JOURNAL.md"
        }
      ],
